  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "title",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# DubSar IDE — Storage Fragmentation Simulation\n",
        "\n",
        "This notebook simulates **storage block fragmentation** using a 7D particle model:\n",
        "\n",
        "| Dimension | Meaning |\n",
        "|-----------|---------||\n",
        "| pos.x | Block address in address space |\n",
        "| pos.y | Logical track / sector |\n",
        "| pos.z | Layer (HDD platter, SSD die) |\n",
        "| mom.x | Migration velocity (defrag direction) |\n",
        "| mom.y | I/O access rate |\n",
        "| mom.z | Wear level rate |\n",
        "| scalar | **Fragmentation index** (0=contiguous, 1=fragmented) |\n",
        "\n",
        "**Tribe A** (green) — Database blocks, should stay contiguous  \n",
        "**Tribe B** (red) — OS/swap blocks, naturally scattered  \n",
        "**Free** (yellow) — Unallocated space, chaotic motion"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "init",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["%%dubsar init-storage 100000"],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "id": "step-note",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Run the Simulation\n",
        "Each step advances the simulation by 16ms (60 FPS equivalent).\n",
        "Tribe particles are attracted to their centroid; free blocks dissipate."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "step-100",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["%%dubsar step 100"],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "render-1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["%%dubsar render"],
      "outputs": [],
      "execution_count": null
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "id": "stats-1",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": ["%%dubsar stats"],
      "outputs": [],
